CONTEXT Twins INCLUDES Registry FROM "../contexts/registry.adl" AS North,
                       Registry FROM "../contexts/registry.adl" AS South
CONTEXT Twins IN ENGLISH
PURPOSE CONTEXT Twins
{+ One context is included twice, under two aliases.
It remains one context with one database, so `North.Person`, `South.Person` and `Registry.Person`
are three references to one concept, and `North.name` and `South.name` are one relation. +}

RELATION knows[North.Person*South.Person]
POPULATION knows[North.Person*South.Person] CONTAINS [ ("p1", "p2") ]

RULE sameRelation : North.name = South.name
RULE alsoByName : Registry.name = North.name
RULE named : knows |- North.name;V[Registry.Name*South.Name];South.name~

ENDCONTEXT
